WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.031
Your web app has every feature.

00:00:02.081 --> 00:00:04.254
So why does it still feel like a website?

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:07.081
Native feel comes down to four behaviors.

00:00:07.131 --> 00:00:09.599
First, motion that follows your pointer.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.037
Second, a keyboard that

00:00:11.087 --> 00:00:12.381
always shows where it is.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.103
Third, calm when someone asks for less motion.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.969
Fourth, layouts that mirror for

00:00:17.019 --> 00:00:18.301
right-to-left languages.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.718
Most teams skip them,

00:00:19.768 --> 00:00:21.387
because each one is real work.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.275
Ballmac UI ships all four.

00:00:23.325 --> 00:00:26.393
Ask your AI agent for a dock, and it finds one.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:27.958
One command later,

00:00:28.008 --> 00:00:29.638
the source is in your project.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.483
Change a single token,

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:33.179
and every component follows.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.516
Same row of icons. Now it feels native.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.665
Ballmac UI. Open source, and yours to keep.
